               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 24-year-old male admitted on 04/10/2025 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever. Clinical examination revealed rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Blood tests demonstrated leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasound confirmed acute appendicitis without perforation. The patient was resuscitated with intravenous fluids and commenced on intravenous antibiotics. On 05/10/2025, he underwent laparoscopic appendectomy without intraoperative complications. The postoperative course was uneventful. Vital signs remained stable throughout. Wound care was performed daily, and adequate analgesia was maintained. The patient was mobilised early and discharged home on 09/10/2025 in good general condition. Please ensure follow-up in approximately two weeks for wound inspection and histology results review. Should any concerns arise, do not hesitate to contact our surgical department.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
